diff --git a/docs/model-file.md b/docs/model-file.md
index 971c6eb..1e5d8c2 100644
--- a/docs/model-file.md
+++ b/docs/model-file.md
@@ -69,6 +69,26 @@ python3 tools/convert/convert.py --sections-from Qwen3.8-FN-UD-Q4_K_XL.basalt --
 `--mtp-dense FILE` (the `mtp/dense` bytes of an official NVFP4, UD-IQ1_M, UD-IQ2_XS or UD-IQ3_XXS pack) swaps in a tuned drafter layer; the converter
 records it in `meta.mtp.dense`. Output is about 122 GiB (123 GiB for the 8-bit variant). The base's vocabulary must be NVIDIA's.
 
+## Native Strata inputs (custom build)
+
+This branch can import a prepared Strata NVFP4/Q8 pack directly, retaining expert bytes and the original drafter:
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/convert/convert.py --gguf qwen-nvfp4-gptq-dense.gguf \
+    --strata-pack pack --ple-gguf ple-fp8.gguf --embd-gguf token-embd-bf16.gguf \
+    --strata-mtp mtp --draft-vocab mtp/draft_vocab.bin --out model.basalt
+```
+
+The native expert index must be v3. Gate/up may be NVFP4 or Q8_0 and down may independently be either; the converter
+checks every mixed expert's scale tail, geometry and file bounds. The PLE must be a scaled E4M3 table with a finite,
+positive `strata.ple.scale`; the embedding must match the dense model and be BF16. Hadamard Gyro experts are not supported.
+Packs record `required_engine_features`: `fp8-ple` and `mixed-nvfp4-q8`. Use this custom runtime, not stock v0.4.0.
+
+Legacy DeepSeek split GGUFs with separate Engram tables use `--engram-gguf TABLE.gguf`. The converter canonicalizes
+integer hash metadata and layer offsets, joins the contiguous table views, aliases `engram_wkv` to `engram_kv`, and
+folds the stored query/key gates into FP32 products. Expert and table payloads remain unchanged. This is separate from
+quality qualification against the original checkpoint; a readable output or kernel parity test alone does not establish it.
+
 ## Qwen3.8-27B pack
 
 The published pack comes from QUASAR's quantization-aware NVFP4 checkpoint
